  <title>The programs it needs</title>
  <p>The bricks are programs that Virtualbricks runs: the VDE programs for
  the switches, the links and the interfaces of this computer, and QEMU for
  the virtual machines. On Debian and Ubuntu they come in these
  packages:</p>
  <table frame="all" rules="rows">
    <thead>
      <tr><td><p>Package</p></td><td><p>Programs</p></td></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><p><sys>vde2</sys></p></td><td><p><cmd>vde_switch</cmd>,
      <cmd>vde_plug</cmd>, <cmd>dpipe</cmd>, <cmd>vde_plug2tap</cmd>,
      <cmd>vde_pcapplug</cmd>, <cmd>wirefilter</cmd>, <cmd>vdeterm</cmd>,
      <cmd>unixterm</cmd></p></td></tr>
      <tr><td><p><sys>vde2-cryptcab</sys></p></td><td><p><cmd>vde_cryptcab</cmd>,
      for the tunnels</p></td></tr>
      <tr><td><p><sys>vde-netemu</sys></p></td><td><p><cmd>vde-netemu</cmd>,
      for the Netemu links</p></td></tr>
      <tr><td><p><sys>qemu-system-x86</sys></p></td><td><p><cmd>qemu-system-x86_64</cmd>
      and <cmd>qemu-system-i386</cmd></p></td></tr>
      <tr><td><p><sys>qemu-utils</sys></p></td><td><p><cmd>qemu-img</cmd>,
      which reads and makes the disk images</p></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>No distribution ships <cmd>vde_router</cmd>, the program of the
  router.</p>
  <section id="where">
    <title>Where Virtualbricks looks</title>
    <p>Each project has a folder for the QEMU programs and one for the VDE
    programs, in its settings: choose <guiseq><gui>File</gui>
    <gui>Settings</gui></guiseq>, then the page of the project. A program that
    isn't in its folder is looked for in the folders of <sys>PATH</sys>.</p>
    <p>Under each folder, the <gui>Settings</gui> window says what it holds:
    the version of QEMU and its programs, and whether the programs of the
    bricks are there, or which one is missing and the package that has it. A
    folder that doesn't exist is an error, and <gui>OK</gui> stays greyed
    until it is fixed.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="missing">
    <title>When a program is missing</title>
    <list>
      <item><p><gui>New Brick</gui> shows a warning sign on the kinds whose
      program is missing, and says which one.</p></item>
      <item><p>At start, Virtualbricks warns about the programs it can't
      find. <gui>Missing programs</gui>, in the settings of this computer,
      turns the warning off.</p></item>
      <item><p>A brick whose program is missing doesn't start, and the
      <gui>Logs</gui> window says why. Install the package, and start it
      again.</p></item>
    </list>
  </section>
